From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:10:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Send no stop command after a failed single-block
 transfer

After a failed single-block transfer the card has already left the data
phase, so the manual CMD12 arrives in transfer state, fails as an
illegal command and shows up in the next card status.

Send the stop only for SDIO extended transfers, for requests with a
stop command attached and for multiple-block transfers.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; on the board with an
eMMC, HS400 tuning fails the EXT_CSD read at every delay outside its
window, and no "send stop command failed" is logged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index 6ae07a72b31b..f854e1b5e4e7 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -506,6 +506,21 @@ static void sunxi_mmc_dump_errinfo(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host)
 		);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A failed transfer needs a stop command only while the card may still be
+ * in its data phase: SDIO extended transfers, transfers the core attached a
+ * stop command to, and multiple-block transfers. After a single-block
+ * transfer the card is back in transfer state, and a CMD12 there is an
+ * illegal command.
+ */
+static bool sunxi_mmc_needs_manual_stop(struct mmc_request *mrq)
+{
+	if (mrq->cmd->opcode == SD_IO_RW_EXTENDED || mrq->stop)
+		return true;
+
+	return mrq->data->blocks > 1;
+}
+
 /* Called in interrupt context! */
 static irqreturn_t sunxi_mmc_finalize_request(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host)
 {
@@ -522,7 +537,8 @@ static irqreturn_t sunxi_mmc_finalize_request(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host)
 
 		if (data) {
 			data->error = -ETIMEDOUT;
-			host->manual_stop_mrq = mrq;
+			if (sunxi_mmc_needs_manual_stop(mrq))
+				host->manual_stop_mrq = mrq;
 		}
 
 		if (mrq->stop)
